# Example requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Start the stack first: make up. Sent mail appears in Mailpit: http://localhost:8025
@base = http://localhost:3000

### Transactional email with an idempotency key (202; repeat it → 200 with the same id)
POST {{base}}/v1/emails
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: reset-ayse-1

{"template": "password_reset", "to": "ayse@example.com", "vars": {"name": "Ayşe", "reset_url": "https://example.com/reset/abc"}}

### Status of one email (use the id from above)
GET {{base}}/v1/emails/REPLACE-WITH-ID

### Bulk campaign: one request, up to 1,000 recipients
POST {{base}}/v1/emails/bulk
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "template": "campaign_report",
  "shared_vars": {"campaign": "Sonbahar", "unsubscribe_url": "https://example.com/u"},
  "recipients": [
    {"to": "a@example.com", "vars": {"impressions": "1200"}},
    {"to": "b@example.com", "vars": {"impressions": "830"}}
  ]
}

### Batch progress (use the batch_id from above)
GET {{base}}/v1/batches/REPLACE-WITH-BATCH-ID

### Validation: missing template variable → 422
POST {{base}}/v1/emails
Content-Type: application/json

{"template": "password_reset", "to": "x@example.com", "vars": {"name": "A"}}

### Make Mailpit reject every recipient with 451 (temporary) — set Probability to 0 to stop
PUT http://localhost:8025/api/v1/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{"Recipient": {"ErrorCode": 451, "Probability": 100}}

### Replay dead-lettered emails (after a 550 made some fail)
POST {{base}}/admin/dlq/replay?limit=100
X-Admin-Token: dev-admin-token

### Metrics
GET {{base}}/metrics
